    </article>
    <article class="reader-panel heritage-dossier" id="rameswaram">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / AN ISLAND OF PILGRIMAGE</p><h2>Rameswaram</h2>
      <dl class="journal-facts"><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Ramanathapuram district, Tamil Nadu, on Rameswaram island</dd></div><div><dt>A shrine to explore</dt><dd>Ramanathaswamy Temple, where Shiva is worshipped as a jyotirlinga</dd></div><div><dt>Story connection</dt><dd>Local traditions of Rama’s worship of Shiva</dd></div></dl>
      <p>The Ramanathaswamy Temple is known for its long corridors and carved pillars. Its sacred setting connects the worship of Shiva with traditions of Rama and the journey to Lanka.</p>
      <h3>A meeting of devotional worlds</h3>
      <p>The district’s official account records the belief that Rama sanctified the place through worship of Shiva, and identifies its importance to both Shaiva and Vaishnava devotees. This is a local sacred tradition, distinct from the ocean-crossing chapter followed in our Hanuman reader.</p>
      <p>Read Hanuman’s journey for the search for Sita, then explore Rameswaram as a place where Ramayana memory and Shiva worship meet. The connection invites comparison without placing every local tradition into the same textual account.</p>
